<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<job id="recruitment-scorecard-prompt" xmlns="http://xmlns.jcp.org/xml/ns/javaee" version="1.0">
    <!--
    Recruitment Scorecard Prompt Job (V531)

    Purpose:
    Ask each assigned interviewer for their scorecard shortly after the
    round actually ENDED (scheduled_at + duration_minutes), while the
    impression is still intact. The FIRST ask, not a chase.

    Why it exists:
    Until V531 the only ask was the daily SLA sweep's overdue nudge,
    which fires 24 h after the interview STARTED and is swept once a day
    at 07:00 UTC - so in practice the first ask landed 24-48 h after the
    meeting. Measured on production 2026-08-24 across all 19
    SCORECARD_SUBMITTED events: mean 24.9 h after the meeting ended, 7 of
    19 over 24 h, and ZERO submitted before the meeting ended (so nobody
    scores live, and prompting afterwards takes nothing away).

    Not extra pressure:
    Every prompt appends SCORECARD_PROMPTED, which counts toward the same
    recruitment.sla.max-scorecard-nudges budget as SCORECARD_NUDGED. This
    job moves the first ask earlier; it does not add one. The daily sweep
    remains the late safety net for anyone who ignores it.

    Window:
    Interviews whose end is between recruitment.sla.scorecard-overdue-hours
    ago and recruitment.sla.scorecard-prompt-minutes ago. The upper bound
    is measured from the END so a round that runs over does not get its
    interviewer pinged in front of the candidate. The lower bound hands
    older interviews back to the daily chase - and stops the first run
    after deploy DMing every interviewer about every un-scorecarded
    interview in the history of the table.

    Quiet hours:
    Nothing goes out before 07:00 or after 20:00 Copenhagen. A 19:00
    interview would otherwise be prompted at 20:20. Suppressing costs
    nothing: the sweep re-derives from source, so the 07:00 run picks the
    pair up, still inside the 24 h window.

    Skipped by construction: cancelled interviews, decided applications,
    interviewers who have already submitted, and any pair already
    prompted or nudged. All side effects are gated by
    recruitment.interviews.enabled (off = no-op).

    Schedule:
    Every 15 minutes via BatchScheduler - a prompt that means "you just
    finished" cannot ride a daily job - gated by
    dk.trustworks.recruitment.scorecard-prompt.enabled (default true).
    Most runs do nothing.

    Similar to:
    recruitment-sla-sweep.xml (the P17 daily sweep, same service, same
    delivery discipline and the shared nudge cap)
    -->

    <listeners>
        <listener ref="jobMonitoringListener"/>
    </listeners>

    <step id="send-recruitment-scorecard-prompts">
        <listeners>
            <listener ref="stepProgressListener"/>
        </listeners>

        <batchlet ref="recruitmentScorecardPromptBatchlet"/>
    </step>
</job>
